        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Myrtus, Eustoma\n- Concepts: flowering plant genera, plant families, common names, taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- Linnaeus described the flowering plant genus Myrtus in 1753.\n- Myrtus is commonly known as myrtle.\n- Myrtus is a genus of flowering plants in the family Myrtaceae.\n- Eustoma is commonly known as lisianthus or prairie gentian.\n- Eustoma is a small genus in the gentian family.",
